WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.751 --> 00:00:08.630
After days of negotiation,
for the very first time,

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:11.591
my parents allowed me
to step out unescorted

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:13.635
for a movie with my friends.

00:00:13.677 --> 00:00:16.888
I was 14 and beyond excited

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.766
with this new freedom I had.

00:00:19.808 --> 00:00:23.311
With a big smile on my face,
I ended up at the back of the theater.

00:00:24.354 --> 00:00:27.023
And just ten steps from my seat,

00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:30.652
I felt these heavy hands
grab both my breasts.

00:00:30.652 --> 00:00:33.321
And before I knew it,
these hands disappeared.

00:00:34.322 --> 00:00:36.324
I screamed and ran outside.

00:00:37.158 --> 00:00:39.995
And I still remember
those dirty handprints

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:42.706
on my white, crisp cotton shirt,

00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:45.542
announcing to the world
what had just happened.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.753
I returned home devastated,

00:00:48.795 --> 00:00:53.258
kept the lights on all through the night
and the outdoors terrified me.

00:00:54.134 --> 00:00:55.885
I didn't want to go out at all.

00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:01.349
It is not news that women
face rampant violence inside homes as well

00:01:01.391 --> 00:01:02.642
across the world.

00:01:03.351 --> 00:01:08.315
So if it's unsafe outside and inside,
where do we go?

00:01:09.441 --> 00:01:14.863
Women in India
are over 600 million strong.

00:01:14.863 --> 00:01:16.531
That's a lot of people.

00:01:16.531 --> 00:01:19.075
But this is what my country looks like.

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:20.368
The outdoors.

00:01:20.368 --> 00:01:22.829
You can count the number
of women in these pictures.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:26.082
And there aren't any, or just one or two.

00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:27.751
And this is by the day.

00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:31.171
But this number
significantly drops at night.

00:01:31.212 --> 00:01:33.423
You don't see many women
walking alone at night

00:01:33.465 --> 00:01:35.800
because they're simply not safe.

00:01:36.301 --> 00:01:41.931
400,000, that's 45 women every hour,

00:01:41.973 --> 00:01:43.725
face varying degrees of violence,

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.478
ranging from domestic violence
to rape in India.

00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:51.107
A 13-year-old girl and her mother
were gang-raped on a highway

00:01:51.107 --> 00:01:53.985
just 45 minutes
from where my parents live.

00:01:55.236 --> 00:01:56.488
When I heard this,

00:01:58.281 --> 00:02:00.867
I just recalled the same incident
that happened to me.

00:02:01.993 --> 00:02:03.411
I was devastated.

00:02:03.953 --> 00:02:06.081
I found myself
in the same hysterical state

00:02:06.122 --> 00:02:07.916
I was outside of that theater.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.378
For everybody around me, life moved on.

00:02:12.712 --> 00:02:16.257
We are hardwired to think
that this is just how the world is.

00:02:16.299 --> 00:02:18.843
Instead of asking the fundamental question

00:02:18.885 --> 00:02:20.470
of how wrong this is.

00:02:21.221 --> 00:02:26.017
I'm here and I'm fighting
for safer spaces for women

00:02:26.059 --> 00:02:28.520
by increasing their mobility,

00:02:28.561 --> 00:02:33.733
by movement of the body and mind
to take control over their lives.

00:02:35.193 --> 00:02:37.237
So how I did that.

00:02:38.571 --> 00:02:43.076
I wanted to prove to the world
that I can face my demons.

00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:48.289
And not just for one,
but 230 continuous days.

00:02:48.331 --> 00:02:53.294
So I decided to walk
across the length of India

00:02:53.336 --> 00:02:56.131
from the very south to the north,

00:02:56.172 --> 00:02:59.175
a distance of 2,300 miles.

00:02:59.217 --> 00:03:00.844
(Applause)

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.348
2,300 miles. How much is that?

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.852
If you started from LA,
you would reach New York.

00:03:08.893 --> 00:03:12.814
If you started from Stockholm,
you would reach Cairo.

00:03:12.814 --> 00:03:14.774
That's the distance that I walked.

00:03:14.774 --> 00:03:17.736
And mile after mile, as I walked,

00:03:17.736 --> 00:03:22.699
it became very apparent
that women's lack of mobility

00:03:22.699 --> 00:03:28.288
hinders their freedom to earn an income
and exert any form of independence.

00:03:29.664 --> 00:03:31.666
On my long walk,

00:03:31.708 --> 00:03:35.503
I wanted to understand what made India

00:03:35.545 --> 00:03:38.631
one of the most
unsafe countries in the world.

00:03:38.673 --> 00:03:40.550
I was determined to meet the women

00:03:40.592 --> 00:03:43.386
who are facing challenges
around their safety.

00:03:43.428 --> 00:03:47.056
And above all, I wanted to understand
if the situation is beyond repair.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:52.520
So I walked through 170 cities,
small towns and villages,

00:03:52.562 --> 00:03:55.774
and I met over 85,000 women,

00:03:55.774 --> 00:03:58.735
in small huddles to, like, large crowds.

00:03:58.735 --> 00:04:00.111
This is a workshop.

00:04:00.111 --> 00:04:04.949
This is with women of an organization
in small huddles inside their homes.

00:04:05.742 --> 00:04:10.705
And that's when I realized
that mobility plays a very, very big role

00:04:10.747 --> 00:04:15.960
in their freedom to pursue
anything outside of their homes.

00:04:16.753 --> 00:04:19.422
When I was walking across the country,

00:04:19.464 --> 00:04:22.258
in my conversations with these women,

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.720
I was talking to them
about different topics.

00:04:25.762 --> 00:04:31.267
And this ranged
from being financially independent

00:04:31.309 --> 00:04:36.189
to taking defensive positions
in times of physical assault.

00:04:36.731 --> 00:04:41.236
This is an activity we did where we want
to anchor ourselves and find our ground,

00:04:41.236 --> 00:04:43.196
and if somebody comes, you push.

00:04:43.196 --> 00:04:44.864
Or just feel stronger.

00:04:44.864 --> 00:04:47.242
What it feels in your body to be stronger.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:52.747
And most of the times our discussions
were around finding your voice.

00:04:52.789 --> 00:04:55.625
(Video) (Speaking Hindi)

00:04:56.793 --> 00:04:59.295
(Together) Aaah!

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:09.472
I wanted women to move with their bodies
and to shift their minds.

00:05:09.514 --> 00:05:11.808
The media amplified our cause

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:17.772
and reported with new energy
on a demand for a safer country for women.

00:05:17.772 --> 00:05:21.317
On my long walk, I met so many people.

00:05:22.485 --> 00:05:28.408
And most of the times,
I noticed that marriage in India

00:05:28.408 --> 00:05:31.244
is treated a little differently
from the rest of the world.

00:05:31.244 --> 00:05:32.537
You see, marriage means

00:05:32.537 --> 00:05:35.540
a woman becomes the property
of her husband and his family.

00:05:35.582 --> 00:05:39.669
And not being able to step outside
to pursue an education, a job,

00:05:39.711 --> 00:05:42.213
or create a community of her own,

00:05:42.255 --> 00:05:45.550
that's lack of mobility,
both social and physical,

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:50.471
that is what reflects the state
of gender inequality in our society.

00:05:51.347 --> 00:05:53.683
On my long walk, I bore witness

00:05:53.725 --> 00:05:57.645
to chilling, violent,
incomprehensible human behavior.

00:05:57.687 --> 00:06:03.401
But at the same time, I met brave women,
survivors of atrocious crimes

00:06:03.401 --> 00:06:08.364
who lit my path with their
unbelievable strength to carry on.

00:06:08.907 --> 00:06:11.409
And then something miraculous happened.

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:13.494
I met this woman named Jai Bharathi.

00:06:14.329 --> 00:06:17.916
On her motorcycle, she arrived
in the same village I was in,

00:06:17.957 --> 00:06:22.921
and she was there at a training camp,
teaching other women how to ride scooters.

00:06:22.962 --> 00:06:25.715
I had never seen
anything like this before.

00:06:25.757 --> 00:06:29.761
She donned the narrative
of being fierce, the odd one out,

00:06:29.802 --> 00:06:34.182
smashing patriarchy every single time
she rode her motorcycle.

00:06:34.223 --> 00:06:38.811
She was an inspiration
for all women, young and old.

00:06:38.853 --> 00:06:40.188
And at the training camp,

00:06:40.188 --> 00:06:44.442
I saw how revving a motorbike
and holding a steering wheel

00:06:44.442 --> 00:06:47.028
didn’t [justt] give these women
the ability to drive

00:06:47.028 --> 00:06:50.740
but that much needed control
over their lives.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:56.663
And I knew instantly
that having women take charge

00:06:56.663 --> 00:06:58.331
and create change for themselves

00:06:58.373 --> 00:07:02.835
is the only way
to transform our broken systems.

00:07:02.877 --> 00:07:07.507
It got me thinking: What if we could
get communities of women moving,

00:07:07.548 --> 00:07:10.718
actually physically moving
away from the house?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.223
That would open a window
where they could move psychologically,

00:07:15.264 --> 00:07:21.020
where they could understand or realize
that she could step out of bad situations

00:07:21.062 --> 00:07:23.147
and have the ability to do it.

00:07:23.147 --> 00:07:27.443
This way we would have
more women feel safe and confident.

00:07:28.486 --> 00:07:31.781
So Jai Bharathi and I, we both decided

00:07:31.781 --> 00:07:35.493
that we are going to join forces
and create a movement

00:07:35.493 --> 00:07:37.787
exclusively for women,

00:07:37.787 --> 00:07:39.414
focused on mobility.

00:07:39.414 --> 00:07:45.211
We have set up a system where a woman
can train to drive for themselves

00:07:45.253 --> 00:07:47.422
or for Ubers, taxis,

00:07:47.463 --> 00:07:51.843
or just become delivery agents
for Amazon and other big companies

00:07:51.884 --> 00:07:53.386
or local businesses.

00:07:53.428 --> 00:07:55.304
That's money in the bank.

00:07:55.346 --> 00:07:58.391
And the freedom
and the psychological, you know --

00:07:58.433 --> 00:08:02.520
know that I can step outside of my home.

00:08:02.562 --> 00:08:06.232
We are connecting these women drivers
on a national network

00:08:06.232 --> 00:08:08.693
where they can reach out
to each other for support

00:08:08.693 --> 00:08:10.319
and to share experiences.

00:08:10.319 --> 00:08:11.696
And not just that.

00:08:11.696 --> 00:08:16.034
She can actually ping
another driver in her vicinity

00:08:16.034 --> 00:08:19.704
if she is feeling distressed,
if she's in danger,

00:08:19.704 --> 00:08:22.915
or if she’s simply just waiting
for her next ride or pickup

00:08:22.957 --> 00:08:24.959
and doesn't want to wait alone.

00:08:25.001 --> 00:08:29.630
For us, receiving our first paycheck
might be very empowering.

00:08:29.672 --> 00:08:32.008
But for 59-year-old Nagamani

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:37.138
that moment arrived when she
put her scooter on a center stand

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.891
and feeling physically strong,

00:08:39.932 --> 00:08:43.561
and proving to the society
that she's beyond being just a sidekick.

00:08:43.603 --> 00:08:47.523
We have trained 1,800 women
who are road ready.

00:08:47.523 --> 00:08:48.566
(Applause)

00:08:48.566 --> 00:08:49.817
And raring.

00:08:54.197 --> 00:08:56.240
Road ready and raring to go.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:01.329
And our decade-long mission is
to bring one million women into mobility

00:09:01.329 --> 00:09:05.374
and be the largest network
of women drivers connected to each other.

00:09:05.917 --> 00:09:07.835
By rethinking mobility for women,

00:09:08.586 --> 00:09:12.548
giving them a safe transport
and safety outside of home,

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:15.426
it is our hope to transform our culture.

00:09:16.219 --> 00:09:20.389
Apart from having a profound impact
on the Indian economy,

00:09:20.431 --> 00:09:23.226
this is about something much bigger.

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:28.481
As you all know,
when we move, we can be seen.

00:09:29.941 --> 00:09:33.528
The more women
see other women in public spaces,

00:09:33.528 --> 00:09:38.491
the more safe, independent
and empowered each one of us will be.

00:09:39.992 --> 00:09:41.369
So.

00:09:41.369 --> 00:09:46.582
If we can learn how to walk,
certainly we can learn how to fly.

00:09:46.624 --> 00:09:47.875
Thank you.

00:09:47.959 --> 00:09:54.924
(Applause)

